{"strongs": "H2918", "word": "טִירָה", "translit": "ti.rah", "root": "טירה", "morph": "H:N-F", "pos": "noun feminine", "gloss": "encampment, battlement", "definition": "[ טִירָה ] noun feminine encampment, battlement (from idea of surrounding , enclosure; Syriac sheepfold , ἔπαυλις ) — construct טִירַת Song 8:9 טִירָתָם Ps 69:25 plural טִירוֺת Ezek 46:23 suffix טִירֹתָם Num 31:10 ; Gen 25:16 טִירוֺתָם 1Chr 6:39 טִירוֺתֵיהֶם Ezek 25:4 — 1. encampment , especially of circular encampment of nomad tribes, mentioned with חצר Gen 25:16 with ערים Num 31:10 ; Ezek 25:4 (|| מִשׁכניהם ); encampment (poetry) = habitation Ps 69:26 (|| אהליהם ); more generally, 1Chr 6:39 (|| מושׁבות ). 2. in metaphor כָּ֑סֶף ׳ ט Song 8:9 a battlement of silver. 3. row of stones, only plural טִירוֺת Ezek 46:23 , virtually plural of טוּר 1 , q. v.", "definition_html": "<h1><entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB3323')\">BDB3323</entry> [<entry onclick=\"sn('H2918')\">H2918</entry>]</h1><div class=\"navigation\"><entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB3322')\">BDB3322</entry> | BIBLICAL HEBREW | <entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB3324')\">BDB3324</entry></div><p> [<bdbheb>טִירָה</bdbheb>] <b>noun feminine</b> <highlightword>encampment, battlement</highlightword> (from idea of <highlight>surrounding</highlight>, enclosure; Syriac <placeholder2085/> <highlight>sheepfold</highlight>, <grk>ἔπαυλις</grk>) — construct <bdbheb>טִירַת</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Song 8:9\" b=\"22\" cBegin=\"8\" vBegin=\"9\" cEnd=\"8\" vEnd=\"9\" onclick=\"bcv(22,8,9)\">Song 8:9</ref> <bdbheb>טִירָתָם</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Ps 69:25\" b=\"19\" cBegin=\"69\" vBegin=\"25\" cEnd=\"69\" vEnd=\"25\" onclick=\"bcv(19,69,25)\">Ps 69:25</ref> plural <bdbheb>טִירוֺת</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Ezek 46:23\" b=\"26\" cBegin=\"46\" vBegin=\"23\" cEnd=\"46\" vEnd=\"23\" onclick=\"bcv(26,46,23)\">Ezek 46:23</ref> suffix <bdbheb>טִירֹתָם</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Num 31:10\" b=\"4\" cBegin=\"31\" vBegin=\"10\" cEnd=\"31\" vEnd=\"10\" onclick=\"bcv(4,31,10)\">Num 31:10</ref>; <ref ref=\"Gen 25:16